---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const faqs = [
  ['How much do TaxDome and Financial Cents cost?', 'TaxDome prices by active clients, billed annually: from $1,500 a year at the 150-client minimum (about $0.83 per client a month), with 20 seats included. Financial Cents: Solo $19/mo (one user), Team $49/user/mo and Scale $69/user/mo on annual billing ($69 and $89 billed monthly, 5-user minimum).'],
  ['How does each handle uncategorized QuickBooks Online transactions?', 'TaxDome lists a Bookkeeping Hub that connects client GLs and manages uncategorized transactions as part of the platform. Financial Cents charges for its Month-End Close (MEC) add-on: $5 per client per month billed annually, on any plan.'],
  ['Which is cheaper for a 3-person firm with 20 review clients?', 'TaxDome at the 150-client minimum: $1,500 per year (~$125 per month), seats included. Financial Cents Team: $1,764 in seats plus $1,200 MEC = $2,964 per year (~$247 per month). At larger client counts TaxDome volume bands apply; check taxdome.com/pricing.'],
  ['Which is better for a solo bookkeeper?', 'Without close review, Financial Cents Solo ($228 per year) costs far less than TaxDome\'s $1,500 annual minimum. With close review on 20 clients, Financial Cents Solo + MEC is $1,428 per year vs TaxDome $1,500 — nearly the same, with TaxDome including a broader tax/portal feature set.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="TaxDome vs Financial Cents for bookkeeping firms: pricing and uncategorized transactions"
  description="TaxDome vs Financial Cents: per-active-client vs per-seat pricing, billing terms, client portal and uncategorized-transaction review (Bookkeeping Hub vs the Month-End Close add-on). Prices verified Nov 2026, with solo and 3-person, 20-client cost math."
>
  <h1>TaxDome vs Financial Cents</h1>
  <p>Both are practice management for accounting firms, and both help review uncategorized QuickBooks Online transactions with clients. The difference is how you pay. TaxDome prices by active clients (from $1,500/year at a 150-client minimum, 20 seats included) and bills annually, with a Bookkeeping Hub in the platform. Financial Cents has cheaper per-user seats and a Month-End Close (MEC) add-on charged per client. Small teams with few review clients often pay less on Financial Cents; firms that want tax + portal + Hub in one annual bill often land on TaxDome.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/taxdome`}>TaxDome</a></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/financial-cents`}>Financial Cents</a></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Firms doing tax and bookkeeping that want one branded client portal and app, billing and workflows, with transaction review in-platform</td><td>Small bookkeeping firms that want low seat prices, client task follow-ups, and close review they pay for only on the clients that need it</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pricing (verified Nov 2026)</td><td>From $1,500/yr billed annually (starts at 150 active clients, about $0.83/client/mo); 20 seats included; volume bands above 150. Add-ons: AI $200/mo, Managed Client Care $100/mo, Premium support $249/mo.</td><td>Solo $19/mo (one user); Team $49/user/mo; Scale $69/user/mo on annual billing ($69 and $89 billed monthly, 5-user minimum). All plans are 12-month agreements.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Uncategorized transactions</td><td>Bookkeeping Hub: connect client GL, manage uncategorized transactions (listed on TaxDome pricing feature set)</td><td>MEC add-on on any plan: $5/client/mo billed annually, for QuickBooks Online</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Client side</td><td>Client portal and mobile app, secure chat, organizers and intake forms, e-signatures; white-labeled app as a paid add-on / Custom</td><td>Client portal and client tasks with automatic follow-ups</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tax work</td><td>Tax organizers, return delivery, IRS transcripts (listed on TaxDome feature set)</td><td>Workflows and deadlines; no tax-specific portal features like organizers or transcripts</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Seats</td><td>20 seats included; unlimited seats via Custom pricing</td><td>Priced per user (Solo = 1 user)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cost at list prices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>3 people, 20 clients needing transaction review. TaxDome: $1,500 per year at the 150-client minimum (~$125 per month), seats included. Financial Cents Team: 3 × $49 × 12 = $1,764, plus MEC 20 × $5 × 12 = $1,200, total $2,964 per year.</li>
    <li>Solo bookkeeper, 20 clients. Financial Cents Solo + MEC: $228 + $1,200 = $1,428 per year. TaxDome: $1,500 per year at the minimum. Without close review, Financial Cents Solo is $228 vs TaxDome $1,500.</li>
    <li>At larger client counts TaxDome volume bands apply (FAQ examples on taxdome.com/pricing: 400 clients $4,125/yr; 1,000 $9,000/yr). Re-check the calculator before you decide.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose TaxDome</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You review uncategorized transactions and want that inside the same tax-and-bookkeeping portal.</li>
    <li>You also do tax work and want organizers, IRS transcripts and return delivery in the same system.</li>
    <li>You can pay annually and want up to 20 seats included.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose Financial Cents</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You are a solo or small team and only a few clients need close review, so per-client MEC plus a cheap seat costs less than TaxDome's annual minimum.</li>
    <li>You do bookkeeping, not tax, and want lower seat prices.</li>
    <li>You want monthly billing and have at least 5 users (still a 12-month agreement).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>Sources: taxdome.com/pricing checked 2026-11-06; financial-cents.com/pricing checked earlier Oct/Nov 2026 sessions. No sponsor has paid for this comparison.</p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/compare/taxdome-alternatives`}>TaxDome alternatives</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/financial-cents-alternatives`}>Financial Cents alternatives</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/taxdome-vs-karbon`}>TaxDome vs Karbon</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/xenett-vs-financial-cents`}>Xenett vs Financial Cents MEC</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/uncategorized-transactions-tools`}>Uncategorized transactions tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
